LBreakout2 for the web (Emscripten / WebAssembly)
=================================================

Building
--------
Install the Emscripten SDK (https://emscripten.org/docs/getting_started/),
then from the top-level source directory:

  source /path/to/emsdk/emsdk_env.sh
  make -f emscripten/Makefile

The result is in build-web/: index.html, index.js, index.wasm and
index.data (the game data). Serve the directory with any static web
server, e.g.

  make -f emscripten/Makefile serve      # http://localhost:8080/

Opening index.html directly from disk (file://) does not work.

Continuous deployment
---------------------
.github/workflows/web.yml builds the web version on GitHub Actions and
deploys build-web/index.* to Cloudflare Pages on pushes to main/master
(pull requests are only built). It needs the repository secrets
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN (permission "Cloudflare Pages: Edit") and
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID; the project name is taken from the variable
CLOUDFLARE_PROJECT_NAME (default: lbreakout2). The project is created on
the first deployment if it does not exist.

How the port works
------------------
- The web build uses SDL2, SDL2_mixer and libpng from Emscripten's ports.
  gui/stk.c/stk.h contain a small SDL 1.2 compatibility layer that is
  active when compiling against SDL2 (SDL_SetAlpha, colour keys, key
  states, unicode, event filter, ...). The game still draws into a 16bit
  software surface which is copied to the canvas on every display update.
  The native autotools build keeps using SDL 1.2 as before.
- The game's blocking loops are kept as they are and compiled with
  ASYNCIFY: every display update waits for the browser's next animation
  frame, SDL_Delay() and SDL_WaitEvent() sleep without blocking the page.
- Config, highscores, saved games and custom levels live in
  /home/web_user/.lgames which is stored in the browser's IndexedDB. It is
  written every few seconds, when returning to the main menu, when the
  page is hidden and when the game is quit.
- Network play is not available (no NETWORK_ENABLED); browsers cannot
  open the plain UDP sockets it uses.
- Text input assumes a US keyboard layout for shifted characters.
- Fullscreen ('f' or Graphics/Display) uses the browser's Fullscreen API
  for the whole page. Browsers allow it only right after a key press or
  click, so the game always starts windowed.
- In game the mouse pointer is locked to the canvas after the first click;
  press Escape to release it.
